# Alert TITLES this investigator declines at its event door: the families it
# has no instrument for. One full-match regex per line; `#` starts a comment.
# Hot-read on every event. A line that is not a regex is logged and ignored —
# the list fails open, because a typo must not silently stop every
# investigation.
#
# Copy to decline-patterns.txt beside this file (gitignored: the real list
# names real alert families) and set, in the deployment's .env,
#   HOOKPROBE_DECLINE_PATTERNS=/etc/hookprobe/operator/decline-patterns.txt
# — the production compose mounts this directory there, read-only.
#
# Why decline rather than investigate and report "unreachable": the platform
# upstream excluded these families from deep analysis on 2026-09-01 for exactly
# this reason, and the pipe's escalation leg funded twenty investigations of one
# of them the following week — 70% of the investigator's bill — each ending in
# a report that could only restate the alert.
\[MAIL\].*
\[QUEUE\].*
ExampleCloud_ManagedDB_.*
